10. Cheatsheet
---

* `klist` - see your ticket
* `kinit` - get new ticket
* `auks -g` - get ticket in cache
* `auks -a` - push current ticket into cache
* `sinfo` - see status of nodes
* `sinfo -o "%10N  %4c  %10m  %35G"` - see CPUs, memory and GPUs for each node
* `squeue` - see queue of jobs including running ones
* `srun command arg1 arg2 ...` - run command in the foreground
* `sbatch <script>` - run a script in the background
* `--nodelist=gpuN` - to request job runs on a particular machine
* `--gres=gpu:<gpu-name>:<amount>` - to request a particular type of gpu, specify it in your gres flag. Current available gpu types are nvidia_rtx_a5000, nvidia_a100-pcie-40gb, nvidia_l40s and nvidia_rtx_pro_5000_blackwell (this is also the default ordering if gpu type is unspecified)
* `scontrol show jobs <job-id>` - see info about submitted job
* `scancel <job-id>` - cancel job
* `du -hs ~/` - to see how much space you have taken up
* `sacct -o "JobID,JobName,AllocTRES%80,State,ExitCode"` - to see recently run jobs
* `df -k` - list mounts and mount points
* `ps -ef` - view all processes running on machine
* `ps -ef | grep <pid>` - find process id info, user is first column
* `getent passwd <username>` - get full name of username
